Z||000000||firstfiero||12-18-2000||08:39 AM||||      I just stopped and looked at a fiero thats for sale and it had me kinda confused. It said it was an 88 but it wasn't a fastback....They didn't make notchbacks in 88 did they? Their was no markings on the back. It said formula across the bottom of the door but I don't think it was a formula. It does have a v6 at least the sticker says it does. I didn't see any other formula markings. the steering wheel was after market and so were the rims.  It also had the smaller wedge nose.....He wants 2400 which seems way to much. it has over 100,000 miles on it.  86se||||reg||3
Z||000001||DrRodey||12-18-2000||08:50 AM||||They DID make notch backs in 88.. both the formula and the coupe were of that style.  The part that is confusing me is that you said it had the 2m6 sticker on it... they discontinuted putting those on in Either 85 or 86.  That is an easy piece to add on though too.  and all Formulas did have the formula sticker on the lower of the door panels.  <P>Depending on the condition, and area that you are in, 2400 might not be all that bad of a price for a good Formula.  <P>------------------<BR>'88 Formula CONVERTABLE<BR>'85 Coupe<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/files/fieroPage.JPG">     <BR> <A HREF="http://freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html" TARGET=_blank>freepages.ugo.com/RodeysPlace/HomePlace.html</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||12-18-2000||08:54 AM||||The "2m6" stickers were dropped after the '86 model year.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||12-18-2000||08:56 AM||||Just check the VIN The Formula and the coupes  in 88 look alike. The coupe is 4 cyl and Formulas are 6 cyl and have Formula stickers on the doors.<BR>Formula<P>------------------<BR> <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_1.gif"> <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
Z||000004||firstfiero||12-18-2000||10:47 AM||||    sorry if you mis understood....Their was no sticker on the back except for the word fiero. I just didn't realize that they still made the notchback in 88. 86se||||reg||12
Z||000005||JBGehling||12-18-2000||12:21 PM||||Just for clarification the Fastback was only produced for the 86-88 GT models. Everything else was notchback.<BR>Josh<p>[This message has been edited by JBGehling (edited 12-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||KissMySSFiero||12-18-2000||01:23 PM||||hey firstfiero<BR>on the formulas, they all came stock with a spoiler.  also  in 88's look for the matrix type trim plates.  not the solid ones.  also if you go to the dealer tell him to pop the trunk and look at the engine.  maybe youll get a funny look....then hell see the engines not under the hood then he can just look dumb.  hehe  and yes IMHO 2400 is too much unless it has t-tops or the rims really look good on it. good luck<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE  88FORMULA<BR>KissMySSFiero@netzero.net<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg"> ||||reg||3
Z||000007||Fformula88||12-18-2000||05:28 PM||||For $2400, it better have a great interior with few to no flaws and a great finish left on the paint job.  That is too many miles for that price if the car isn't in really good condition.  Also, be sure to look underneath for rust.  Its ok if there is a little surface rust, but be sure the floor pans and such aren't rotting out yet (you'll know, it will be very obvious).  Also, to be sure it is an 88 Formula, check the VIN and options label on the front drivers side wheel well.  <P>The 88 Formula VIN should read...<BR>1G2PE1195JP------  The "E" means Formula and the "9" is the V6 engine.<P>The options tag should  have the following listed...<BR>D80 (rear spoiler, standard on 88 Formula's)<BR>PHO  (15 inch "GT" style diamond spoke wheels)<BR>WS6  (Performance suspension)<BR>L44  (2.8L V6 HO)<P>Good luck on your Fiero sewarch, and if you give him an offer try to get it a lot lower than his asking price!<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000008||firstfiero||12-18-2000||06:14 PM||||    I already decided to stay away when I saw it had one of those little s***** pep boys sun roofs. It was in good condition inside and out. The interior was worn but no holes or anything...the rims were in average shape. I was also turned off by the fact it's an automatic.  Thanks for the help....86se||||reg||1
